/F2 13 Tf 50 665 Td (1. ABSTRACT) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 0 -18 Td (Robotics and automation technologies are becoming increasingly important in modern engineering.) Tj
0 -14 Td (This project focuses on the design and implementation of a voice-controlled robot with obstacle) Tj
0 -14 Td (detection capability using the Arduino platform. The robot is controlled through Bluetooth using) Tj
0 -14 Td (the HC-05 module connecting to a smartphone application. Commands are processed by an Arduino Uno) Tj
0 -14 Td (microcontroller driving high-torque DC motors via an L298N dual H-bridge motor driver.) Tj
0 -14 Td (To ensure collision safety, an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor continuously profiles front clearance.) Tj
0 -14 Td (If an obstacle is detected within 20 cm, the robot automatically applies electronic braking.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 0 -30 Td (2. INTRODUCTION & PROBLEM STATEMENT) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 0 -18 Td (Traditional remote-controlled robots depend entirely on human operators. If reaction time lags,) Tj
0 -14 Td (collisions occur. Furthermore, manual joysticks lack natural accessibility for disabled users.) Tj
0 -14 Td (This project eliminates manual controllers by introducing natural speech recognition coupled with) Tj
0 -14 Td (continuous autonomous obstacle sensing, achieving a safe, cost-effective, and user-friendly system.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 0 -30 Td (3. PROJECT OBJECTIVES) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 0 -18 Td (- Design an intuitive voice-controlled robotic platform responsive to natural speech.) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Establish stable wireless Bluetooth RF communication between mobile devices and Arduino.) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Implement bidirectional motor control for forward, reverse, left, right, and stop motion.) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Integrate ultrasonic distance measurement with automatic emergency collision stoppage.) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Deliver an open, modular platform for educational robotics and embedded systems learning.) Tj
ET
